LOGBOOK.md:8:### 0315 — Receive-window credit is bounded by one value-semantic ledger (TASK-260715-3kimon)
LOGBOOK.md:10:- IMPLEMENTATION: Core selects control, ordinary, capped-BDP bulk, and relay control-plus-UDP-burst initial windows with checked configuration and saturating arithmetic. Initial and earned adjustment credit reserve per-channel, per-lane, global-window, and global-ledger capacity before admission; releases are exact and idempotent.
LOGBOOK.md:15:### Cross-layer memory authority separates reservation from physical evidence (TASK-260715-1pn983)
LOGBOOK.md:17:- DECISION: One checked-byte ledger owns packet, HEV, SSH, DNS, client relay, rekey, metrics, and reconnect admissions. SSH credit is separate from resident bytes but reserves permitted local storage; failed reads are unknown, never zero or absence.
LOGBOOK.md:19:- DNS RESIDUAL: The hard candidate ledger is 7,635,554 bytes inside an 8,388,608-byte component budget. Combined with the accepted 9,715,712-byte incremental HEV/bridge peak, it leaves 8,110,080 bytes in the lower 25 MiB engineering envelope. This proves arithmetic fit only; production remains false pending complete physical composition.
LOGBOOK.md:21:- GAPS: Final watermarks, BDP/window winners, component ceilings, untracked reserve, overlap, and iPhone rows remain evidence-gated. No Apple guarantee, payload capture, flow migration, or weakened gate is asserted.
LOGBOOK.md:26:- EVIDENCE: Public-API bridge, IPv4/IPv6 framing, deterministic faults, hostile-frame fuzzing, bounded pressure, lifecycle, packaging, notices, and physical Mac MTU/memory rows trace to accepted task-scoped resources in `docs/TASK-260715-2jatnd_m0-bridge-hev-decision-adr.md`. The worst measured incremental HEV/bridge cost was 9,715,712 bytes at 500 sessions; whole-extension SSH/DNS/relay/cache/reconnect memory remains unmeasured.
LOGBOOK.md:28:- GAPS: Physical iPhone, jetsam, NAT64, sleep/wake, energy, and whole-extension memory stay deferred/blocked and are never inferred from macOS. M1 consumers may use this baseline only through the exact accepted-outcome binding task; production composition remains fail-closed on its other M0 inputs.
LOGBOOK.md:33:- ROOT CAUSE: The rev3 gate coupled two distinct claims. Harness-owned channels, reads, queues, boundary/native lifecycle counters, and descriptor-close stages were released deterministically, but the gate still required Darwin to return allocator pages during the same 500-cycle observation. One reviewer run therefore failed on a bounded `+180224 B` non-decreasing footprint rise while the next two passed.
LOGBOOK.md:34:- FIX: The schema-2 lifecycle evidence now records an `ownedResourcesReleased` verdict and every underlying ownership field for each cycle. The production gate requires 500 cycles, zero failed owned-resource-release cycles, and the unchanged post-warmup maximum resident-footprint drawup ceiling of `256 KiB`. Monotonic and late rises remain classified with exact transition/cycle evidence, but OS page-return timing is no longer used as a proxy for product-owned release. The matrix atomically emits its exact-tree-bound raw report before returning a failing verdict.
LOGBOOK.md:35:- NEGATIVE EVIDENCE: Production-call-site tests reject 499 cycles, a footprint overflow, and one missing owned-resource release at cycle 499. A separate emission-order test proves the raw-evidence closure runs before the production gate throws. Forged working-tree and HEV artifact provenance remain fail-closed.
LOGBOOK.md:44:- INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 2000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. The sampler observed both rises and releases, including `-1,196,032 B` and `-1,130,496 B` segments; post-warmup net change was `-2,310,120 B`. Across the last 500 samples, net change was `-65,536 B` and range was `98,304 B`. Descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed within `6...8`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. Earlier 500- and 1000-cycle repeats still had late rises, proving neither duration alone established convergence.
LOGBOOK.md:46:- ANOMALY/FIX: The first extended attempt stopped at cycle 257 with Swift signal 5 because the test payload used checked `UInt8(iteration)`. `UInt8(truncatingIfNeeded:)` removes that artificial 255-cycle harness limit while address and port continue to identify each flow. The 2000-cycle investigation passed in 106.74 seconds. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.
LOGBOOK.md:51:- STOP: Three independent 100-cycle physical-Mac probes all failed the corrected gate: `+81,920 B` with `4/85/0`, `+81,920 B` with `5/84/0`, and `+98,328 B` with `4/85/0` increase/equal/decrease transitions. Per rev3 instructions, the 100/250/500 matrix and full suite were not run against a known failing lifecycle prerequisite, and the rule was not weakened. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.
LOGBOOK.md:54:- MEASUREMENT: A physical Mac15,9 (arm64, macOS 26.5) SwiftPM run admitted 100, 250, and the explicitly narrowed 500-session ceiling with zero bridge drops. Physical footprint was 12,354,160 B, 15,270,512 B, and 20,038,256 B; peak was 20,054,640 B. The incremental 500-session HEV/bridge cost was 11,976,704 B, leaving 19,480,576 B inside the provisional 30 MiB envelope. This is not a whole-extension Apple guarantee and does not allocate SSH, DNS, relay, caches, or reconnect overlap.
LOGBOOK.md:55:- LIFECYCLE: One hundred real HEV start/traffic/stop cycles restored descriptors, sessions, queued batches, outstanding reads, boundary start/stop ownership, and HEV/bridge close stages; sampled physical footprint did not grow monotonically. Seven startup and seven cleanup cancellation stages plus 50 harness host-termination iterations passed.
LOGBOOK.md:56:- AVAILABILITY: `os_proc_available_memory` is explicitly unavailable on macOS in the public SDK. HEV queued bytes and process-wide Swift task counts also have no public gauge. All are recorded as unavailable/unknown; host memory, process threads, and proxy zeros were not substituted. Physical iPhone and sleep/wake remain named deferred gaps.
LOGBOOK.md:57:- PRESSURE: Real stalled-path pressure accounts every send or bounded drop and cleans up. Soft/pressure/critical ordering remains deferred until SSH admission integration because the current memory-pressure seam is advisory and has no production policy consumer; no global pressure tool was invoked.
LOGBOOK.md:59:- REV2 AUTHENTICITY: Every final raw run is fail-closed on an exact candidate tree OID and reads the pinned HEV revision/source SHA-256 from `NativeDependencies/manifest.json`. Each emitting run performs and serializes its own 100-cycle descriptor/thread/session/read/queue/physical-footprint samples and derives monotonic growth from those values. The original signal 6 came from the retired `proc_pid_rusage` importer; the final sampler uses public `task_info(TASK_VM_INFO)` plus `proc_pidinfo(PROC_PIDTASKINFO)` and is exercised by three independent exact-tree runs.
LOGBOOK.md:124:- GATES: Every M0 viability row maps evidence for both candidates. libssh2 has no waived red row; ReluxNIOSSH's missing neutral TCP ownership, opaque signer, bounded intake, algorithm reporting, keepalive, and unbuilt adapter rows remain explicit. The four deferred semantics remain unsupported/notReported under `TASK-260728-3cveay`; physical scale, extension memory, soak, and DNS footprint remain M3 gates.
LOGBOOK.md:125:- MEASUREMENT: Five consecutive current-tree, already-built real-OpenSSH M0 lifecycle runs exit 0 in 11.058–11.144 s test time. Whole-command maximum RSS is 71,254,016 B and maximum macOS peak footprint is 17,891,952 B; every lifecycle iteration asserts zero channels, socket, session, automatic tasks, custom allocations, and buffered bytes. This is a controlled harness envelope containing direct-tcpip, not an isolated DNS-open p99 or physical extension budget.
LOGBOOK.md:185:- IMPLEMENTATION: The test now injects `ManualFixtureClock`, waits until the first queued open has registered its 300 ms timer, and advances exactly 300 ms to preserve the pre-admission timeout assertion. It then keeps the clock fixed while the second open queues and rekey resumes, removing wall-clock scheduling from the success boundary without extending a timeout, sleeping, skipping, or weakening the expected error.
LOGBOOK.md:191:- VERIFICATION: The four lifecycle regressions pass together 30/30 consecutive focused runs. A final reset-on-any-failure streak passes 20/20 unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs with 427 tests in 35 suites per run and 16–18 second durations, including historical runs 13, 16, and 17. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, warning-free recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The sshd listener set before and after remains the same older PIDs 1330 and 34815.
LOGBOOK.md:200:- ROOT CAUSE: Independent run 16 passed the repaired caller-cancellation case, then hung in `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey`. A socket failure or close race in the transport-owned keepalive entered `handleOperationFailure`, awaited fatal teardown, and teardown attempted to drain that same `automaticKeepaliveTask`. This self-join parked both the keepalive and `transport.close`; the injected `ManualFixtureClock` made teardown's otherwise bounded timer remain suspended and exposed the cycle deterministically. This supersedes the earlier assumption that only the cancellation fixture's two remote sleeps caused the aggregate hang.
LOGBOOK.md:206:- ROOT CAUSE: The real-sshd cancellation test opened two `sleep 2` exec channels while injecting a `ManualFixtureClock`. Caller cancellation correctly detached the pending read, but the following channel disposal still had to advance libssh2 cleanup behind the bridge-owned POSIX service and remote process exit. Because the manual clock also owned the channel-close deadline and was no longer advanced, cleanup could not expire independently; suite completion depended on two wall-clock subprocess lifetimes and could hang when socket/sshd retirement lost the favorable scheduling race. A clean baseline measured 4.116 seconds for this test, matching the two sequential sleeps.
LOGBOOK.md:218:- DEFERRED GAPS: Receive-window consumer credit/cap, RFC channel-open reasons, exact exec-exit/core-dump metadata, and deep server-rekey/keepalive observability remain explicit `unsupported` or runtime `notReported`, owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`. Physical scale, memory, and soak remain separate M3 rows; no exact value was inferred from the C fixture's 16 observed server-KEX transitions.
