LOGBOOK.md:673:- VERDICT: Changes requested and routed to `analysis`. Original hostile fixture, DNS equality/one-over, canonical hashes, warning-free diagram, 57 task references/50 titles, byte-identical copies, board/diff/privacy checks, and all 332 Swift tests otherwise pass. Evidence: `TASK-260715-2kchi0_re-review-01-verdict-20260722.md`.
LOGBOOK.md:679:- VERIFICATION: Board/schema/fixture/task-reference/copy/privacy/diff/render/XML checks pass; the warning-free PlantUML SVG was visually inspected; all 332 Swift tests in 29 suites pass. No benchmark was run and no tuning candidate or production DNS value was authorized.
LOGBOOK.md:684:- DECISION: Protocol v1 fixes synthetic workload generation, ten deterministic seeds, controlled impairment profiles, warmup/steady/cooldown schedules, sampling, paired bootstrap and practical-effect rules, non-tradeable byte/DNS/route/resource/memory/failure/drop/cleanup gates, content-addressed raw references, capture authorization, privacy classes, and immutable pass/red/unavailable/invalid outcomes before tuning begins. macOS named-device rows are current; iPhone slots are schema-compatible deferred rows and are not guessed from Mac evidence.
LOGBOOK.md:686:- GATE: DNS candidate limits remain non-authoritative with `productionAuthorization.permitted=false`. Production use still requires accepted selected-SSH `direct-tcpip` timing/footprint/cleanup evidence (`TASK-260715-1gjxer`), the ADR-009 residual DNS component budget (`TASK-260715-1pn983`), physical-provider startup/footprint rows, and independent review.
LOGBOOK.md:829:- CORRECTION: Full DNS/TCP wire accounting now reserves 65,537-byte read and write buffers for a 65,535-byte message plus its two-byte prefix. Corrected candidate ledgers are 3,686,706 and 7,635,554 bytes. Exact maximum success, one-byte-over rejection, split prefix/body, partial write, and coalesced frames are exercised.
LOGBOOK.md:832:- STOP-LINE: The 4/8 MiB and timing figures are non-authoritative candidates. ADR-014 lacks accepted selected-SSH `direct-tcpip` rows (`TASK-260715-1gjxer`), and ADR-009 lacks an accepted residual DNS component ledger (`TASK-260715-1pn983`). Machine policy sets `productionAuthorization.permitted=false`; ADR-022 and all downstream consumers remain blocked pending those inputs, physical provider rows, and independent review.
LOGBOOK.md:835:- EVIDENCE/DECISION PROPOSED: Default policy is 4 endpoints, exact 65,535-byte DNS messages, 16 live owners, 256 KiB queued wire, 4 MiB aggregate DNS, and 2/5/30/8/10-second open/response/logical/startup/idle values; hard envelope is 8 endpoints, 32 owners, 1 MiB queue, 8 MiB aggregate, and 5/10/120/40/30 seconds. The full-wire message value is fixed rather than tunable so memory policy cannot truncate legitimate DNS/TCP responses.
LOGBOOK.md:836:- ACCOUNTING: Default/hard ledgers are 3,686,704/7,635,552 bytes and include encoded request, maximum response, three TCP prefixes, one retry request, 1,024-byte correlation/tombstone state, 64 KiB read/write/manager/diagnostics reservations, queue, and endpoint table. Startup and logical deadlines cover every serial endpoint slice by equation; inconsistent field combinations fail closed.
LOGBOOK.md:837:- MEASUREMENT: Three main fixture runs plus three isolated default/hard memory runs passed IPv4/IPv6/dual/unreachable/malformed/stall/concurrent-failure/cancellation/M2 semantics, zero resolver calls, byte-for-byte allocation, zero FD delta, and zero tracked live bytes. Maximum isolated incremental physical footprint was 3,653,656/7,749,656 bytes. The controlled loopback results validate mechanics and bounds, not production SSH latency.
LOGBOOK.md:869:- RESOURCE: Adapter capacity is an atomic non-waiting reservation bounded by the HEV session ceiling and the measured M0/SSH/Core memory equation; exact flow, chunk, queue, window, and timeout values remain injected measurement inputs for M1/M3 rather than promoted constants. Diagnostics are aggregate schema-v1 only and exclude credentials, SOCKS bytes, endpoints, hostnames, payloads, and flow identifiers.
LOGBOOK.md:930:- BASELINE: The fixture now tracks tasks, timers, sockets, channels, and retained dependencies separately. One hundred factory generations restore every counter plus the coordinator's internal task/resource footprint; thirty-two concurrent starts produce one usable publication, and thirty-two repeated stop/health race generations clean each owned resource exactly once.
LOGBOOK.md:937:- COVERAGE: Deterministic direct and concurrent stop-wins tests assert one stopping-to-disconnected publication cycle, repeat-stop idempotency, no configuration load/settings/capability publication, no external resources, and the internal baseline footprint. The concurrent test pauses snapshot publication after the terminal state is recorded, allowing a competing start to enter during the in-flight stop without a production test hook.
LOGBOOK.md:943:- COVERAGE: A package-internal async handoff hook, following the existing core test-hook pattern, deterministically injects current-generation DNS health loss after child completion and independently pauses the same boundary for caller cancellation. Neither test issues a masking `stop()`; both assert no capability revival, exactly-once reverse cleanup, a zero external resource ledger, and the coordinator baseline footprint.
LOGBOOK.md:960:- DECISION: `RuntimeDiagnosticsStore` owns one bounded generation with 96 counters, 56 gauges, one cumulative DNS-latency histogram, and at most one cataloged error per each of 10 finite domains. Packet/HEV use its `TunnelMetrics` recorder, SSH uses the same recorder without lane identity, and coordinator/TCP/DNS/route/memory use typed finite-category updates; unknown free-form metric names are counted then discarded without retaining the label.
LOGBOOK.md:962:- PRIVACY: The default schema has no lane/run/flow IDs, DNS or destination fields, addresses, credentials, commands/stdin, payload content, or traffic samples. State transition times are monotonic process-uptime milliseconds; errors retain only validated domain/code; flow, memory, route, health, packet/byte, drop-reason, DNS-result, and SSH values are aggregates.
LOGBOOK.md:1034:- FINDING: swift-format baseline is zero-warning; first emitter draft produced 36 lint warnings (line length, numeric grouping, single-element trailing comma). Emitter now emits lint-clean Swift (multi-line struct literals, `_`-grouped literals ≥7 decimal/≥8 hex digits, chunked parity strings); repo-wide `swift format lint` back to 0.
LOGBOOK.md:1070:- VERIFICATION: Design verified against production code: `waitForReadCallCount(N+1)` is a strict happens-after for batch N drop accounting — pump awaits `recordDrop` (summary emitted synchronously in the metrics actor, `PacketFlowBridge.swift:1224-1271`) before the next `readPackets()` resumes waiters; `stop()` joins pumps before `flushDropSummary` (`PacketFlowBridge.swift:1012-1045`). Injected `ManualTunnelClock` alone drives the 10s window; `eventually{}` removed; `sleepCallCount == 0` asserted. Intent strengthened, not loosened: exact per-window counters (would_block=2 first summary, no_buffer=1 stop flush, no carryover).
LOGBOOK.md:1083:- NOTE: Pinned upstream checkout and C sources untouched; script rendered in memory from checksum-verified content. Review evidence: board outcome `BUG-260720-2zh86a_review.md`.
LOGBOOK.md:1087:- FIX: The verified HEV build script is rendered in memory from manifest minima and executed without modifying the pinned checkout or C sources. Every retained HEV slice now targets iOS/tvOS 18.0 or macOS 15.0; ReluxLibSSH2 triples, OpenSSL flags, CMake targets, artifacts, and locks now target iOS 18.0/macOS 15.0. Inspection rejects unmodeled XCFramework slices.
LOGBOOK.md:1148:- VERIFICATION: Two clean source rebuilds produced byte-identical XCFramework locks; checksum/allowlist/tamper, public-symbol, notice, static/extension-safe, strict C warning, Swift packaging, 64-test core, and `swift build` gates pass. The local OpenSSH fixture observed 14 server-KEX transitions, including a deliberate failure, plus measured reply RTT and a deterministic timeout/miss.
LOGBOOK.md:1227:- DECISION: ADR-014 remains open. Both candidates retain identical host-key, window, sustained 5 GiB rekey, scale (through 1,000 channels), cancellation, algorithm, extension-build, memory, and physical-size gates. Unknowns are named experiments in `.research/260720_task-260715-28ok1k-ssh-engine-candidate-audit.md`; no missing capability was waived.
LOGBOOK.md:1242:- VERIFICATION: The emitted in-memory YAML records caller MTU, `udp: tcp`, task stack 24576, TCP buffer 4096, `udp-copy-buffer-nums: 2`, and max sessions 1200. The generator rejects any stack input the pinned parser would silently raise.
